      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JEDI DREAM (7) disappointed in the Gimcrack but was much better in the Karrakatta and Sires' before the break. She's trialled nicely coming into this and the aid of an inside barrier is ideal for her as she'll be right in the firing line from the beginning. Down in the weights and is the most appealing with her upside. LET'S TALK (3) was just fair two back before winning narrowly at Belmont last start off a freshen. Things look to shape similarly this time with Tsang's claim coming in handy. Ticks a few boxes and can repeat the dose without surprising. SUPERSMASH (9) couldn't bring up the hat-trick before a 3.1L defeat in Open 3YO company most recently. She remains down in the weights as she comes back in grade today and she maps for a beautiful run in transit. Can get back to winning ways. KRAKEN TIME (2) can improve coming back in trip and with a small change with his gear. HEZANGELIC (1) trialled nicely coming in and can make an impression first-up.",
